    "done_when": "Done when. tests/test_a_request_that_has_not_launched_is_not_drawn_working.py feeds a follower fixture pointers for three requests with no pid and no launched_at , one each in phase queued , held and awaiting-upstream , plus one launched run with a pid. It finds classify_pointer classifying none of the three as running, and finds the three drawn in their own phases and counted outside the working column, and only the launched run drawn and counted as working. At the base revision the same test finds at least one of the three drawn as working. A second case launches the queued request (writes its pid and launched_at ) and finds it then drawn queued → working . A third case ages the held and awaiting-upstream pointers past the stall window and finds neither reaching needs-you, since no worker exists to stall; a fourth case drops and archives a request (no live pointer remains) and finds it drawn as dropped, never as working, as nova-a8 saw at 18:02Z when all 16 requests of a batch, 13 of them already dropped and archived, drew new → working in the same second; at 16:41:10Z nova-a1's five requests went working → needs you at 55 minutes on that false running classification, with their pointers unchanged and the session's obligations view empty. The negative control draws every non-terminal pointer as working again, and the first case then fails. The test files importing reckon/crew/recovery_watch.py add no failure against the base revision, run on the all_debug partition one arm at a time with at most -n 4 , never on the fleet node. Every log is under the run directory, starts with its revision and the literal command, and ends in EXIT= . Ruff check and ruff format --check add no findings on the staged paths. A second population is the five nova requests of the Why, whose recorded pointers the test reproduces and finds none classified running. Write paths: reckon/crew/recovery_classification.py , reckon/crew/recovery_watch.py , reckon/crew/ticker.py and the new test tests/test_a_request_that_has_not_launched_is_not_drawn_working.py .",
